# Copy this file to .env (repo root) and fill in your own key, OR export
# the same variable in your shell before running uvicorn. Never commit
# the real .env file.
#
# This key is OPTIONAL and separate from frontend/.env.example. It is
# only used by the server-side geocoding proxy (backend/location/geocode.py,
# GET /api/location/geocode and /api/location/reverse) so that a Maps key
# never has to be embedded in the browser at all, for deployments that
# want that extra bit of key hygiene.
#
# If you're fine with a browser-restricted key instead (the simpler,
# default setup -- Places Autocomplete running client-side), you only
# need frontend/.env and can leave this file / variable unset entirely.
# The app runs correctly either way, or with neither set (falls back to
# the simulated Leaflet map).
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=YOUR_SERVER_SIDE_API_KEY_HERE
